`WHISPER_SDL2` is the flag that builds the streaming transcriber, and it also
builds four other programs — talk-llama, command, lsp and wchess. One of them
cannot be built here at all: talk-llama's CMakeLists `FetchContent`s llama.cpp
from github AT CONFIGURE TIME, and this distribution builds with no network by
rule, so the whole configure step ends in `Could not resolve host`.

There is no flag for it. `WHISPER_USE_SYSTEM_LLAMA` is the only escape and it
wants a llama port this tree does not have, so the subdirectory list is what
has to change.

The other three go with it rather than being built and then deleted: a chat
front end, a voice-command demo, a language-server demo and a chess board are
each a program nothing on this desktop opens, and `wchess` installs nothing at
all — minutes of compiling for a file that never reaches the package.

--- a/examples/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/examples/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -111,9 +111,6 @@
     add_subdirectory(parakeet-quantize)
     if (WHISPER_SDL2)
         add_subdirectory(stream)
-        add_subdirectory(command)
-        add_subdirectory(talk-llama)
-        add_subdirectory(lsp)
         if (GGML_SYCL)
             add_subdirectory(sycl)
         endif()
@@ -121,7 +118,3 @@
 
     add_subdirectory(deprecation-warning)
 endif()
-
-if (WHISPER_SDL2)
-    add_subdirectory(wchess)
-endif (WHISPER_SDL2)
